The Film Commission is the only nonprofit organization dedicated to bringing jobs and economic impact to Northeast Ohio through the growth of a sustainable media production industry. Since passing the Ohio Motion Picture Tax Credit in 2009, more than 110 productions have shot in Cleveland, including “The[ Avengers],” “Captain America: The Winter Soldier,” and most recently, Matthew Mc[Con]aughey’s “White Boy Rick” and Helen Hunt’s “I See You”.[]

